course: dictionary
lesson: 12438
title: The decimetre
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A decimetre is a unit of length. It is one tenth of a metre, and it is the same as 10 centimetres. We write it as dm. «The table is 7 dm long» means the table is 70 centimetres long.
explain: The prefix deci means one tenth. That is why a decimetre is one tenth of a metre. A metre has 10 decimetres, and each decimetre has 10 centimetres, so a metre has 100 centimetres.
explain: Decimetres sit between centimetres and metres. Use them to measure things that are too long for centimetres to count easily, but too short to need metres. When you see square or cubic decimetre, the word tells you what is being measured: an area or a volume.
fact: A decimetre is one tenth of a metre.
fact: 1 decimetre = 10 centimetres, and 1 metre = 10 decimetres.
fact: «The box is 2 dm wide» means the box is 20 centimetres wide.
fact: A cubic decimetre is the space inside a cube that is 1 dm on every side, and it holds 1 litre.
fact: In American English the word is spelled decimeter, but it means exactly the same thing.
exercise: «The pencil is 2 dm long.» How many centimetres long is the pencil? | 12 cm | *20 cm | 2 cm | 200 cm
exercise: How many decimetres are there in 1 metre? | 1000 | *10 | 1 | 100
exercise: A box measures 1 dm by 1 dm by 1 dm. How much liquid can it hold? | 1 millilitre | *1 litre | 100 litres | 10 litres
test: What is the short written form of decimetre? | m | *dm | mm | cm
test: Which is longer: «5 dm» or «40 cm»? | They are the same length | Neither, you cannot compare them | 40 cm | *5 dm, because 5 dm is 50 cm
exam: «A rope is 3 dm long. Ava cuts off 1 dm.» How many centimetres of rope are left? | 30 cm | 10 cm | 200 cm | *20 cm
